# Provenance pin for the Tranco popularity snapshot used by the blocklist
# tripwire. The snapshot itself is NOT in this repo -- see the TRANCO_FILE
# comment in build-blocklist.sh for why (Tranco grants no licence, and the list
# it serves carries CC BY-NC and CC BY-SA components). It lives on the build box
# at /var/lib/patanyx-blocklist/tranco-top100k.txt and is regenerated by
# scripts/refresh-tranco.sh.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS. A RELEASE-TIME record: which popularity data the tripwire
# decisions in a shipped version were made against, so a verdict can be
# reproduced or disputed later. Recording a hash of someone's data is not a copy
# of it, which is why this can live in the repository when the snapshot cannot.
#
# WHAT IT IS NOT. A running log of what is on the build box. The weekly
# patanyx-tranco.timer writes to /var/lib/patanyx-blocklist/tranco-history.log
# instead and never touches this file: a root timer appending to a tracked file
# on a release branch produces an unreviewed diff every week, and an automated
# append is not the deliberate record this is meant to be.
#
# UPDATE IT BY HAND, at release, by running scripts/refresh-tranco.sh. The build
# warns when the live snapshot appears in neither this file nor the history log,
# which is the only case that means someone replaced it out of band.
#
# Format: one "<sha256>  <retrieved-date>  <entries>" line, newest last.

cd54a76fcd02c062ce7c50664be888a7ca3bc89b999cea2f3e12ae9f3c08649b  2026-08-10  100000
43a28e6369bc7788d1738832e817b393dd9f73b0f4c520c4d2d2360aab662621  2026-08-10  100000
